  "body": "P0 (#91): a drill with its R plane below the unfaced stock top generated with no warnings and posted silently - the rapid down to R crossed uncut stock.\n\n**Proof (before)**: DR-0400, part top Z20, box stock top Z25, R plane 20, clearance 35 - `status Ok`, `warnings []`; Fanuc `G81 X0 Y0 Z12 R20 F80` / `G73 X0 Y0 Z12 R20 Q12 F80`, Heidenhain `G00 ... Z+20*` - all posted. The drill-reach check cut the stock at R, and verify's rapid law skips vertical rapids (#96).\n\n**What changed** (`crates/app/src/operation/drill_reach.rs`)\n- New `r_plane_clear`: refuses by name, per cycle (every kind), any raw stock above the R plane over the tool's body (the wider of drill and shank): \"R plane Z 20.000 is below the stock top Z 25.000 over the hole at (0.000, 0.000) - the rapid down to R would cross uncut stock (a collision); raise Top of Part Z (the R plane) to the stock top or above (stock faced by an earlier operation still counts at its raw height)\".\n- The depth and holder checks read the full stock height (no longer cut at R) - depth unchanged, the holder check no longer under-counts.\n- Faced-then-drilled stock still counts at raw height (#89) - refused until then; workaround: R at the raw stock top.\n\n**Fixtures that now refuse - all real (their own stock stood over R)**: `drilling_axial` lathe world (box z0..44 over a bar z-20..20 -> box matches the bar), `lathe_post::an_axial_drill_posts_through_the_document_with_the_lathe_post_chosen` (new `lathe_world_at` helper; golden unchanged), `drilling_cross::a_z_only_drill_file_never_writes_the_cross_key` (R 15 under a 44 mm box -> R 44, clearance 50).\n\n**Pinned by** `drill_rplane::{an_r_plane_below_the_unfaced_stock_top_is_refused_by_name, neither_post_releases_an_r_plane_below_the_stock_top, an_r_plane_at_the_stock_top_still_posts_canned_and_expanded}`.\n\n**Gates**: quick gate green; the agent ran drill_rplane, drilling_axial, drill_reach, drill_reach_fit, face_holes, posting, operations, verify, conformance, golden_cl, blind_floor, center_cut_owed, drilling_cross*, lathe_post, lathe_spindle_law, project_roundtrip, solid_law, lib - green; clippy clean.\n\n**Follow-up**: #96 (P0) - verify's rapid law blind to vertical rapids into stock for every operation type.\n\nChangelog: fix(app): drilling refuses by name an R plane (Top of Part Z) below the unfaced stock top - the rapid down to R crossed uncut stock and posted silently\n\nFixes #91\n",
